Mapping: A terminal pinging solution.

DESCRIPTION
Mapping is a lightweight CLI tool that
can ping multiple hosts with the run of a single
command with multithreaded performance.

CONFIGURATION
Mapping can be configured with its configuration file, named 'mapping.conf'.
Here, you can alter the values of the fields to fit your needs:

1. hosts: the list of comma-separated IP addresses or domains to which
a series of ping requests should be sent to.

2. threads: the number of CPU threads to use for performance optimization.

GENERAL USE
In the directory you have downloaded Mapping in, run the command: “python3 mapping.py”. 
Ensure that mapping.conf is in the same directory as the script is.
Mapping will start pinging the hosts you have specified, sometimes multiple at once
if you have indicated a certain number of CPU threads to use for the program's 
execution. After Mapping has successfully ran, it will print out a dictionary 
for each host it tried to ping, indicating the time taken to resolve the host
and any errors that happened in case Mapping could not reach the host. The results
obtained will be written to a JSONL file called "results.jsonl" that includes
a query-ready structure indicating the trials on each line.

